<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Schutzstaffel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1925">1925</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as SS, Protection Squadron</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Schutzstaffel (SS) was a major paramilitary organisation under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-hitler">Adolf Hitler</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nazi-party">Nazi Party</a> in Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Formed from a small bodyguard unit, it officially marked its foundation on 9 November 1925, and under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-himmler">Heinrich Himmler</a>, its leader from 1929 to 1945, it became the foremost agency of security, mass surveillance and state terrorism. Its branches included the Allgemeine SS, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waffen-ss">Waffen-SS</a> and the SS-Totenkopfverbände, which ran the concentration and extermination camps. The SS was the organisation most responsible for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a> of an estimated 6 million <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> and millions of other victims in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holocaust">Holocaust</a>, and at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a> it was judged a criminal organisation.</p></div>
